{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>Which Moses smote, etc., when they came out of Egypt.</b> It is difficult: was it not in the fortieth year that Moses struck the land of Sihon? Perhaps it intends to say that from the time of their departure from Egypt, it was prepared before them to strike it, for had the affair of the spies not occurred, they would have struck it in the second year of their going out from the land of Egypt." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say that from the time Israel came out of Egypt, terrors of death fell upon him from them, and he was stricken and standing — in the manner that the Sages of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 100) that thethe tradition was in their hand, etc. And for this reason Scripture juxtaposed the phrase <b>when they came out</b> to the phrase about the striking, and afterward said ״וַיִּירְשׁוּ אֶת אַרְצוֹ״ to alert you to our words."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The Hebrew reads מָסֹרֶת בְּיָדָם; the text appears partially corrupt or truncated (followed by וכו׳). Transmitted hyper-literally; the non-Hebrew characters in the manuscript fragment have been left as they appear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:16.670800652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}